{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_signals

    "What weighs on the decision": one row per signal, each with an icon of its own shape, the
    number, what it means and a state word, so colour is never alone. Below them the method line,
    the numbers a confirmation does not move.

    The attention line counts the signals that need attention and names the worst; it never says
    what to do, because the plugin sees numbers and the decider judges a person. A red signal
    disables nothing: seats and places warn and never block.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * signalsheading string - the section's heading
    * attentionflagged boolean - whether any signal needs attention, which weights the line
    * attention string - the count naming the worst signal, or the sentence saying nothing is
      over a limit; plain spelling
    * signals array - one entry per signal, each with:
      * label string - what is measured, with its number, plain spelling
      * hasdetail boolean, detail string - what the number means for this decision, plain
      * haslink boolean, href string, linktext string - an anchor into the evidence column
      * isok, iswarn, isover, isread, isnone boolean - the state, exactly one true
      * rowclass string - the row's background, a Bootstrap subtle utility or empty
      * hasstateword boolean, stateword string - the state in a word
    * hasmethodline boolean - whether this reader is told the method's numbers (a decider in the
      course; never a viewer or a mentor)
    * methodline string - applications held, how many deferred and the places without a limit,
      on this method, plain spelling

    Example context (json):
    {
        "signalsheading": "What weighs on the decision",
        "attentionflagged": true,
        "attention": "1 point of attention before deciding: Turma A: 18 of 20 seats taken.",
        "signals": [
            {
                "label": "Turma A: 18 of 20 seats taken", "hasdetail": true, "detail": "Seats left in the key's group: 2.",
                "iswarn": true, "rowclass": "bg-warning-subtle", "hasstateword": true, "stateword": "Attention"
            },
            {
                "label": "Earlier applications to this course: 1", "hasdetail": true, "detail": "The last: Cancelled, 04/06/26.",
                "haslink": true, "href": "#enrol_apply_review_history", "linktext": "See the history",
                "isread": true, "rowclass": "", "hasstateword": true, "stateword": "Read"
            },
            {"label": "No comment from the applicant", "isnone": true, "rowclass": ""}
        ],
        "hasmethodline": true,
        "methodline": "On this method: 52 of 60 applications held; 4 deferred."
    }
}}
<section class="enrol_apply-signals mb-3" aria-labelledby="enrol_apply_signals_heading">
    <h2 class="h5 mb-1" id="enrol_apply_signals_heading">{{signalsheading}}</h2>
    <p class="enrol_apply-attention small mb-2{{#attentionflagged}} fw-semibold{{/attentionflagged}}" data-region="attention">{{attention}}</p>
    <ul class="enrol_apply-signallist list-unstyled mb-2">
        {{#signals}}
            <li class="enrol_apply-signal {{rowclass}}">
                <span class="enrol_apply-signalicon">{{#isok}}{{#pix}}i/valid, core{{/pix}}{{/isok}}{{#iswarn}}{{#pix}}i/warning, core{{/pix}}{{/iswarn}}{{#isover}}{{#pix}}i/invalid, core{{/pix}}{{/isover}}{{#isread}}{{#pix}}i/info, core{{/pix}}{{/isread}}{{#isnone}}{{#pix}}i/info, core{{/pix}}{{/isnone}}</span>
                <span class="enrol_apply-signaltext">
                    <span class="enrol_apply-signallabel">{{label}}</span>{{#hasdetail}} <span class="small">{{detail}}</span>{{/hasdetail}}{{#haslink}} <a class="small" href="{{href}}">{{linktext}}</a>{{/haslink}}
                </span>
                {{#hasstateword}}<span class="enrol_apply-signalstate small fw-semibold">{{stateword}}</span>{{/hasstateword}}
            </li>
        {{/signals}}
    </ul>
    {{#hasmethodline}}<p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0" data-region="methodline">{{methodline}}</p>{{/hasmethodline}}
</section>
